","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anyasabo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anyasabo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anyasabo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anyasabo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2021-02-04T13:52:34Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/775214171","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/52997#issuecomment-775214171","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/52997","id":775214171,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc3NTIxNDE3MQ==","user":{"login":"jakelandis","id":976291,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3NjI5MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/976291?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis","html_url":"https://github.com/jakelandis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-02-08T15:07:21Z","updated_at":"2021-02-08T15:07:21Z","body":"I ran a test of over a weekend from cloud for a HTTPS endpoint with 30m delay between Watches, and experienced no issues. However, I do believe that there is an issue that should be addressed. I think what is happening is that some firewall configurations are force-able closing the connection it see's as idle (Watcher uses HTTP client with a connection pool) and for some reason, the HTTP connection in the pool does not get the memo. \r\n\r\nAnecdotally it is most prevalent talking to Microsoft teams and https://discuss.elastic.co/t/watcher-and-microsoft-teams-webhook/203189 even mentions a `tcp-rst-from-server`. A tcp trace might be in order to once we can reproduce this to see who/what is closing the connection. I don't think this is a Watcher specific error, but maybe there is some HTTP client configuration (version) that would help, or possible we need to handle this kind of error with a retry at the application level.  ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/775214171/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jakelandis","id":976291,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3NjI5MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/976291?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis","html_url":"https://github.com/jakelandis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakelandis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/831995585","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/52997#issuecomment-831995585","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/52997","id":831995585,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgzMTk5NTU4NQ==","user":{"login":"DaveCTurner","id":5058284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNTgyODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5058284?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner","html_url":"https://github.com/DaveCTurner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-05-04T14:41:43Z","updated_at":"2021-05-04T14:41:43Z","body":"> maybe there is some HTTP client configuration (version) that would help\r\n\r\nI think it would help to expose `HttpClientBuilder#setConnectionTimeToLive()` when constructing the HTTP client in `org.elasticsearch.xpack.watcher.common.http.HttpClient#createHttpClient`. Without that I believe we are assuming that a pooled connection remains valid forever, but that appears not to be the case in some environments. I don't think we should change the default from today's behaviour of an infinite TTL.\r\n\r\nI also don't see anything that enables TCP keepalives on these connections. I think we should do that by default on any connection that we expect to remain open for an extended period (relates https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/65213).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/831995585/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"DaveCTurner","id":5058284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNTgyODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5058284?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner","html_url":"https://github.com/DaveCTurner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":4687319763,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDQ2ODczMTk3NjM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/events/4687319763","actor":{"login":"DaveCTurner","id":5058284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNTgyODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5058284?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner","html_url":"https://github.com/DaveCTurner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/following{/other_user}","gists_url"